.TH okf-jawn-list_workspaces 1  "list_workspaces " 
.SH NAME
okf\-jawn\-list_workspaces \- List the workspaces this connection may read, each with its current head revision. Treat head as a pin: pass it to later reads as at = {"kind": "revision", "revision": head} so every call sees one consistent state, and compare it with a later listing to detect change.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBokf\-jawn list_workspaces\fR [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the workspaces this connection may read, each with its current head revision. Treat head as a pin: pass it to later reads as at = {"kind": "revision", "revision": head} so every call sees one consistent state, and compare it with a later listing to detect change.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR [default: http://127.0.0.1:7711]

.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR [default: {}]
JSON request, @file, or \- for stdin
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
